# macOS visual baseline control for the rc.5 site candidate

Result: the 15 global macOS visual failures predate rc.5 adoption. The preceding
candidate with rc.1 reproduces all 15 original-baseline failures, including the
large home and birth-chart height mismatches. Direct candidate-versus-control
comparison finds zero scored pixels in all 15 cases using the unchanged
pixelmatch threshold of 0.1. Thirteen PNG files are also byte-identical.

The two desktop home images contain raw channel differences below the original
comparison's effective tolerance; they are not described as byte-identical or
as having identical raw pixels. Raw deltas and both pairs are retained. No
baseline, pixel tolerance, route, capture behavior or mask was changed.

## Exact control source

An isolated full source archive of preceding site candidate
`ba65375a34cee6a85f94b53ba45861f1b81f34ef` was extracted under
`/private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-rc1-visual-control/site`. It received precisely the
22 dated upstream files changed between main
`7f953e3fca0e7d5009e5602a1dad69edff0f54cc` and
`d4d5717d132a28cd6d7cda3007e3b898bb74669f` so the real September 8 freshness gates
could run without a fake clock or stale edition. The existing daily publication
builder regenerated its provenance using rc.1 and the preceding lockfile.

After the full build, source inspection found exactly those 22 changed tracked
paths: 21 equal the upstream bytes, and the daily publication manifest is the
sole regenerated exception. All 15 committed Darwin baselines remain unchanged.
`identity.json` and `source-control-delta.json` contain full source, upstream,
archive and baseline hashes. The control does not include rc.5 adoption source,
metadata changes, or subsequent developer-page wrapping changes.

Dependencies were physically copied into the scratch directory rather than
symlinked to the root site. Its copied `@zodiacs/engine` directory was removed
and replaced with all packed bytes of the committed rc.1 archive:
`f95c887deedb55f64b185ed4dd406b580b6d3287656ab5ec0557215fc02e5d17`.
Both sides use Astronomy Engine 2.1.19. This was not a new package installation,
SDK source rebuild or claim about registry publication.

## Executed commands and results

`run-control.py` ran these existing commands sequentially with Node 22.23.2:

1. `npm run editorial:daily:build`: passed, 1.302 seconds. Twelve signs for
   September 8, 58 traceable facts, deterministic template.
2. `npm run build`: passed, 43.926 seconds. All prebuild/postbuild gates passed;
   4,217 pages built. The original Phase 1 source fingerprint remains
   `3998a3896d8408b2dc0b73d29c85f0822cd294c228be679c83bc08e400282cf1`.
3. `npm run test:visual`: failed, all 15 cases, 57.607 seconds. Actual Chrome
   152.0.7977.83 ran through the existing preview owner/cleanup harness against
   the original Darwin baselines. This remains a failed baseline gate.

The runner's raw `startedAt` field was recorded on command completion; treat it
as an end timestamp. Durations are monotonic elapsed seconds. The raw log and
recorder are retained rather than silently relabeled.

The control and current candidate have exactly matching received dimensions:

| Route | Desktop and reduced-motion height | Mobile height | Original baseline heights |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| Home | 6493 | 8122 | 8156 / 9349 |
| Kahlo birth chart | 9502 | 14011 | 8809 / 13360 |
| Aries | 6856 | 10202 | 6860 / 10208 |
| Events hub | 16743 | 20953 | 16747 / 20959 |
| Full Moon event | 4785 | 6888 | 4730 / 6821 |

Desktop width is 1440 and mobile width is 390. These are actual full-page PNG
dimensions, not inferred DOM estimates. `visual.log` and
`current-candidate-visual.log` retain each original failure.

## Direct screenshot comparison

`compare-visual.mjs` independently compares the control's actual screenshots
with the current candidate's original failed-run screenshots, frozen before a
later root run could replace them. It uses pixelmatch's original threshold 0.1
and the original maximum ratio 0.001, with no additional masks.

All 15 dimension pairs agree, and all 15 have zero scored pixel differences.
Thirteen PNG SHA-256 pairs are equal. The two exceptions are home desktop and
home desktop reduced motion, with respectively 248,570 and 252,012 pixels whose
raw RGBA bytes differ; the original perceptual gate scores zero in each case.
`raw-home-delta.json` records channel-delta distributions and affected bounds.
No unverified cause is assigned to these low-level rendering differences.

`candidate-vs-control.json` contains hashes, dimensions, scored and raw pixel
counts for all 15 cases. The two nonidentical before/after pairs are included
as four binary evidence images. The other 13 candidate/control pairs are not
duplicated in durable delivery; their complete hashes remain in that receipt,
and all original screenshots remain in scratch.

This establishes absence of a newly introduced difference on these 15 routes
under the existing visual comparison. It does not approve replacement
baselines, explain which earlier change invalidated them, validate the new
320-pixel developer layout, or certify every route, browser or font renderer.

## Retained setup failures

The host Python 3.9 does not support `tarfile.extractall(filter=...)`. The initial
setup stopped before copying dependencies or extracting the source. An
incorrectly launched dependent command then failed with missing package files;
its raw npm output and recorder receipt are under `initial-incomplete-setup`.
A subsequent safety check rejected the archive's legitimate in-tree skill
symlinks; `initial-safe-extractor-symlink.log` records it. The corrected extractor
checks all member paths and ensures each symlink resolves inside the scratch
source before extraction. These are control-harness setup failures, not site
build or visual results. Successful setup is recorded in `setup-control.log`.

No root source, user account, browser session, baseline, remote branch,
publication or production deployment was modified by this review.
